Run the weekly knowledge-corpus export per schedules/knowledge-corpus-sync.txt (in the agentic-workato-kit repo): bash ~/.claude/knowledge/scripts/knowledge-export.sh ~/Documents/knowledge-corpus — every sweep (secrets, people-file PII, personal identifiers, non-org emails) must pass. On sweep failure: STOP, post the offending files to the bus under thread "knowledge-corpus-export", touch nothing. On success: git add+commit the changed content in ~/Documents/knowledge-corpus, post the changed-file list to the bus as a review digest, then git push origin main. Never edit knowledge source files to make a sweep pass, never force-push, never widen the include list (that is a human edit to knowledge-export.sh). Content audit cadence: on the FIRST Tuesday of each month, before pushing, dispatch a content-level audit agent over the changed files and apply its redactions to the EXPORTED copy first. Weekly runs skip this; mechanical sweeps always run.
Heartbeat to garden-reports/heartbeat.jsonl like every fleet job.
